{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggiMj5QEefdJdPKEzXWS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Dq ≈ 1000 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 490 cm⁻¹.** These come from a least-squares fit of the high-spin d⁷ (Co²⁺-like) band energies, and the fit is only approximate.\n\n**Assignment.** The three bands are ν₁ = ⁴T₁g(F)→⁴T₂g, ν₂ = ⁴T₁g(F)→⁴A₂g and ν₃ = ⁴T₁g(F)→⁴T₁g(P). In the same order, they are at 8 620, 18 410 and 20 250 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Model.** Energies are measured from the ⁴T₁g(F) baseline.\n- ⁴T₂g lies at +2Dq and ⁴A₂g at +12Dq.\n- The two ⁴T₁g states mix through the matrix [[−6Dq, 6B], [6B, 15B + 6Dq]]. Its lower eigenvalue E₋ is the ground state and its upper eigenvalue E₊ is the ⁴T₁g(P) state.\n- The transition energies are ν₁ = 2Dq − E₋, ν₂ = 12Dq − E₋ and ν₃ = E₊ − E₋.\n\n**Why a fit is needed.** The model has two unknowns (Dq, B) and three bands. Solving exactly from ν₁ and ν₂ gives Dq = 979 cm⁻¹. Adding ν₃ then gives B ≈ 462 cm⁻¹. That pair is not consistent with the full mixing matrix, so I fitted all three bands together.\n\n**Fit result.** The least-squares fit gives Dq ≈ 1002 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 490 cm⁻¹. The residuals are about −165, +67 and +8 cm⁻¹ for ν₁, ν₂ and ν₃. The Dq of about 1000 cm⁻¹ is typical of Co²⁺. B ≈ 490 cm⁻¹ is about 50% of the free-ion value (roughly 1 000 cm⁻¹ for Co²⁺), a plausible reduction due to covalency.\n\nC is not determined by these spin-allowed bands, so I give no value for it.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1000, \"B\": 490, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Least-squares fit of high-spin d7 Tanabe–Sugano ⁴T₁g mixing to three bands gives Dq≈1000, B≈490 cm⁻¹; C is not determinable from these bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1339,"cache_read_input_tokens":1659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1339,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"st